meta {
  name: Delete the book
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/books/{{bookId}}
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 202
}

docs {
  202, not 204: the storage object, chapters, chunks and the row all go in one Celery
  task, and the actor is carried across so the audit row names a person rather than the
  worker that happened to run it.

  One task on purpose — a half-deleted book is worse than either state: chunks whose
  vectors go on answering questions about material the owner believes is gone.

  This folder runs last because everything above depends on the book existing.
}
